    {
      "id": "53af43309422ed90b1d5cd72788b7d65a294e68b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 589446100,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Ha, they added [their](https://medium.com/swlh/apples-m1-secret-coprocessor-6599492fc1e1) own [instructions](https://gist.github.com/dougallj/7a75a3be1ec69ca550e7c36dc75e0d6f)\n\nYes, I know. Is that forbidden by the terms of an architectural license from Arm - in particular, is it forbidden by the terms of ''Apple's'' architectural license from Arm?\n\nThe AMX instructions are in the first \"Unallocated\" part of the \"Reserved\" part of the A64 instruction set (section C4.1.1 of the v8-A Architecture Reference Manual).  Apple don't publish those instructions; if the Accelerate framework enables them on when called and disables them before returning, and the kernel can keep the \"AMX enabled\" state as part of the thread state, then the only ways to use them are 1) call something in the Accelerate framework or 2) enable them yourself, Apple could just say \"if you do the latter, we make no guarantee that your code will continue to work, don't complain to us if it breaks\", so if Arm were to use that part of the  instruction encoding space in the future, Apple could move the AMX stuff elsewhere and have different implementations of Accelerate for different processors.  If Arm define instructions in the future that could replace the AMX instructions, Apple could use those and, again, have different versions of Accelerate for different processors.\n\n> and [destroyed some protections](https://m1racles.com/) on it too!\n\nYes, Apple silicon has errata, just like other silicon.\n\nAnd, as the author of that page notes, the purpose of the page is \"Poking fun at how ridiculous infosec clickbait vulnerability reporting has become lately. Just because it has a flashy website or it makes the news doesn't mean you need to care.\"",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-05-31T22:42:12.190Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-05-31T22:42:12.190Z",
          "system": false,
